1
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,350
ED1

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,359
What is this? You've got a
huge hole in your window!

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:10,109
That's hardly my fault. I got
attacked by that Lancer guy.

4
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:14,109
Wait. You fought him on your
own before you summoned Saber?

5
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:16,740
Not really. He
just kicked my butt.

6
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:20,619
Not even trying to make
yourself sound good?

7
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:25,000
I see. When it comes to you,
what you see really is what you get.

8
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,000
- Minuten vor Schweißen.
- Minutes before welding.

9
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,320
Tohsaka...

10
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,949
You really are a mage, huh?

11
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,859
You're one too, aren't you?

12
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:51,440
Not really. I can't
do anything like this.

13
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:54,919
What do you mean, you can't?

14
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,949
Working with glass is the
most basic of the basics.

15
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,830
I don't know any of these
"basics" or "fundamentals."

16
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:06,330
Honestly, how did someone like
you manage to summon Saber?

17
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:08,269
Well, whatever.

18
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:11,340
First things first, I need
to repay you for earlier.

19
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:31,320
In the face of absolute despair

20
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,560
{\an8}You don't have any idea what
you're caught up in, do you?

21
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:58,070
To be blunt, you've
been chosen as a Master.

22
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:01,779
Have you noticed a brand
somewhere on your body?

23
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:02,909
A brand?

24
00:03:02,910 --> 00:03:05,070
She is referring to the
Command Spells, Shirou.

25
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:12,919
O-Oh, these?

26
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:16,629
Yes. Those symbolize
your status as a Master.

27
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:19,210
They're also spells
which bind your Servant.

28
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:23,720
So as long as you have those,
you can control your Servant.

29
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:26,350
What do you mean,
as long as I have them?

30
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:29,469
Command Spells
are inviolable orders.

31
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:34,350
They force your Servant's obedience,
even if it means bending them to your will.

32
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:38,360
Saber broke off her
attack earlier, remember?

33
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:44,279
However, you only get three such
orders, so try not to waste them.

34
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:49,369
If you use them all, you'll probably be
killed, so I suggest you exercise caution.

35
00:03:49,370 --> 00:03:50,370
I'll be killed?

36
00:03:50,830 --> 00:03:51,999
That's right.

37
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,250
The Holy Grail War is based around
Masters defeating other Masters.

38
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,823
Whichever Master prevails
over the other six will

39
00:03:59,835 --> 00:04:02,549
win the Holy Grail,
which can grant any wish.

40
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:05,220
Hey, hold on a second. What
do you mean by "Holy Grail"?

41
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:09,260
To cut a long story short,
you've been dragged into a ritual.

42
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:13,100
One called the Holy Grail
War, fought by seven Masters...

43
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,730
a battle to the death
between mages.

44
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:18,440
What the hell are
you talking about?

45
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,819
I'm simply laying out the facts.

46
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:25,200
Besides, it should be obvious
even to you at this point.

47
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:29,450
After all, a Servant nearly
killed you not once but twice.

48
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:32,330
Convinced yet?

49
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:35,000
I was also chosen as a Master.

50
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:38,868
Think of your Servant as
a familiar, granted to you

51
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,750
by the Grail to help you
win the Holy Grail War.

52
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:45,510
She doesn't look much
like a familiar to me.

53
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,339
Of course not.

54
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:49,349
Though they're technically
classed as familiars,

55
00:04:49,350 --> 00:04:53,179
Servants are actually superhuman
beings—heroes from the past.

56
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,929
Heroes from the past?

57
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:55,930
Saber too?

58
00:04:56,310 --> 00:04:57,559
That's right.

59
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,769
Servants are heroes
summoned from legends...

60
00:04:59,770 --> 00:05:04,400
be they ancient or modern—into
our time and given physical forms.

61
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,900
It's the Master's
role to summon them,

62
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:10,660
upon which they are made manifest
through a phenomenon of the Grail.

63
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:15,749
Basically, a Servant is
always with you in spirit form.

64
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:19,920
And should the need arise, you
can make them materialize and fight.

65
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:25,630
So that guy in red can transform at
will between spirit and physical form?

66
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,880
That's Archer.

67
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:30,720
I'm having him keep watch
outside for the time being.

68
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,890
Do you understand
everything so far?

69
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:36,180
The individual words, sure.

70
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,965
If you want a more
detailed explanation, you

71
00:05:38,977 --> 00:05:41,440
should talk to the man
who oversees the Grail War.

72
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:44,690
All I can tell you

73
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,490
is that you have no
choice but to fight,

74
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:52,240
and that Servants are powerful
familiars, so you should use yours well.

75
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,080
Now, then.

76
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:01,750
From what Emiya-kun has said,

77
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:05,499
I gather that you're in an
incomplete state, Saber?

78
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,460
Yes.

79
00:06:06,461 --> 00:06:09,630
As you say, I am not
at full fighting strength.

80
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:12,889
Shirou is not a
full-fledged Master,

81
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:15,390
so even replenishing my
mana is likely to be difficult.

82
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,640
That's surprising.

83
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:21,439
Hey, what are you two
talking about, Tohsaka?

84
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:27,149
Servants maintain their existence
here with mana supplied by their Masters.

85
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:32,279
But because you're a novice, she
can't get mana from you directly,

86
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:34,450
which will make
things difficult.

87
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,080
Would you like some, Emiya-kun?

88
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:38,540
I'm good.

89
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:42,880
I have to admit, I didn't expect
you to be so forthcoming with me.

90
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:48,089
You'd already realized something was wrong,
so there was no point in concealing it.

91
00:06:48,090 --> 00:06:52,299
Given that, I felt revealing our
hand to an enemy such as yourself

92
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:55,890
could help Shirou better
understand our situation.

93
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:59,020
Her disposition's perfect, too.

94
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:04,149
Damn it, that makes it
even more of a waste!

95
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:08,650
If I were Saber's Master, this
war would be as good as won!

96
00:07:09,070 --> 00:07:11,650
Hey, are you saying
I'm not worthy of her?

97
00:07:12,910 --> 00:07:14,660
Of course I am, you hack!

98
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:20,289
Okay, shall we go?

99
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:21,410
Go? Where?

100
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:25,880
To see the man who knows
all about the Holy Grail War.

101
00:07:26,590 --> 00:07:30,010
You want to know what
all this is for, don't you?

102
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,009
Of course.

103
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:34,510
It's kind of late, though.

104
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:37,049
What? Not interested after all?

105
00:07:37,050 --> 00:07:40,519
Well, it's your call.
What about you, Saber?

106
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,519
Leave Saber out of this!

107
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,099
Don't try to strong-arm her.

108
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:47,689
Oh, so you do
think like a Master.

109
00:07:47,690 --> 00:07:49,780
You don't want me
talking to Saber?

110
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:52,279
Why should I care?

111
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:57,030
Damn, I'm starting to feel like
something is wrong with her.

112
00:07:57,490 --> 00:08:01,499
I mean, Saber's a hero
from the past, right?

113
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:05,709
She won't be able to make
sense of the modern world.

114
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:07,750
That isn't true, Shirou.

115
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:11,459
Servants adapt to whatever
era they find themselves in.

116
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:14,549
As such, I am quite
familiar with this time.

117
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:17,259
You're familiar with it? Really?

118
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,429
Of course.

119
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:22,019
This is also not the first time I
have been summoned to this era.

120
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:25,269
No way! What are the odds?

121
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:28,020
Well? Where are we going?

122
00:08:30,730 --> 00:08:33,070
The church in Shinto.

123
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:10,669
What else can we do?
She can't dematerialize.

124
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:13,610
It beats having her walk
around with her armor on display.

125
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:20,569
Hey, are you planning to
walk all the way to the next city?

126
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:21,570
I am.

127
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:24,409
You know it's been
dangerous out lately, right?

128
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:27,619
I can't guarantee your
safety if things go south.

129
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,499
Relax.

130
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:35,760
You may be forgetting, but Saber
over there is ridiculously strong.

131
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,390
Master of Archer.

132
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:47,140
Just call me Rin.

133
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:51,929
In that case, Rin. What was
Shirou trying to say earlier?

134
00:09:51,930 --> 00:09:54,070
I am unable to comprehend it.

135
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,934
Perhaps it was out of
a major misconception,

136
00:09:56,946 --> 00:09:58,570
or just sheer stupidity, but...

137
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:03,580
He was saying that he'll leap
to our rescue if we get attacked.

138
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:07,339
But... Shirou is my Master.

139
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:09,710
Is that not a
reversal of our roles?

140
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,630
He's probably not
thinking that way at all.

141
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:16,880
He couldn't care less about
Masters, Servants, or anything like that.

142
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:19,510
What's that supposed to mean?

143
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,669
Why do you suppose
Saber won't come in with us?

144
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:57,800
She said she's been in
this time period before.

145
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:01,810
So maybe something happened
between her and the phony priest here.

146
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:10,059
Tohsaka, what kind
of guy is this priest?

147
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:12,569
He used to be my father's pupil.

148
00:11:12,570 --> 00:11:16,359
After Father died, he
became my guardian.

149
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:20,580
He and Father taught
me everything I know.

150
00:11:21,330 --> 00:11:24,499
Wait, so this priest
is also a mage?

151
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,579
That's right.

152
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:28,210
He's a certified
phony, that priest.

153
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:34,463
You've accepted none
of my prior invitations,

154
00:11:34,475 --> 00:11:37,470
but here you are now
with an unusual guest.

155
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:40,340
I take it this means
he is the seventh,

156
00:11:40,970 --> 00:11:41,970
Rin?

157
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:49,599
I am Kotomine Kirei.

158
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:54,110
What is your name,
seventh Master?

159
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,610
Emiya Shirou.

160
00:11:57,030 --> 00:11:58,110
Emiya?

161
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:08,119
Then, Emiya Shirou, can I assume you
are the Master of the Saber-class Servant?

162
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:11,249
Yeah, I made a
contract with Saber,

163
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:17,669
but this stuff about Masters and the
Holy Grail War is all nonsense to me.

164
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:20,890
If a Master is supposed
to be a proper mage,

165
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:24,099
you really ought to
pick someone else.

166
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:25,639
I see.

167
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,390
This is serious indeed.

168
00:12:27,850 --> 00:12:30,770
You'll need to start
from square one with him.

169
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:33,440
Very well.

170
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:37,860
This is the first time you have
ever sought my assistance.

171
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,949
Emiya Shirou,

172
00:12:39,950 --> 00:12:43,619
the status of Master
cannot be yielded to another.

173
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:46,990
And, once conferred, it is not a thing
from which one can simply walk away.

174
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:51,119
Being a Master is a trial you
have been chosen to undergo.

175
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:55,380
You will not be freed from that
ordeal until you win the Grail.

176
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:59,377
Emiya Shirou, this battle
you've found yourself

177
00:12:59,389 --> 00:13:02,640
caught up in is called
the Holy Grail War.

178
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:06,890
Some nonsense about seven
Masters fighting to the death, right?

179
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:12,979
It is a ritual meant to select the
one who is worthy to hold the Grail.

180
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:15,638
You keep talking about
this "Holy Grail", but

181
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:18,319
you don't mean the
actual Holy Grail, do you?

182
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,899
The Grail that appears in
this town is the genuine article.

183
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:28,290
For proof, one need look no further
than the unrivaled miracle of the Servants.

184
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:35,039
A Holy Grail capable of this can
surely grant its holder limitless power.

185
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:39,129
In the face of such a fact, the
item's "authenticity" is irrelevant.

186
00:13:39,130 --> 00:13:42,800
Then why force people to go
through this Holy Grail War thing?

187
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:47,049
If it's that powerful,
why not just share it?

188
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:51,809
A reasonable suggestion, but
only one may claim the Grail.

189
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:56,560
We did not make that decision.
Rather, the Grail itself decided it.

190
00:13:57,650 --> 00:13:59,569
The Grail decided it?

191
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:03,239
This is all the work
of the Grail itself.

192
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:07,320
It selects its one true owner by
having the Masters fight to win it.

193
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:10,700
That is the Holy Grail War.

194
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,960
I'm still not convinced.

195
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:18,999
Even if only one can be chosen,

196
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,379
I don't like the idea that that
person has to kill the other Masters.

197
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,380
Hold on.

198
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:26,719
We don't have to kill
each other, Emiya-kun.

199
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:28,219
No, it is a fight to the death.

200
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:30,220
Hush, Kirei!

201
00:14:30,970 --> 00:14:35,899
Listen, the Holy Grail that appears
in this city is a spiritual object.

202
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:39,269
And since it's spiritual,
we can't touch it.

203
00:14:39,270 --> 00:14:40,440
Do you see where I'm going?

204
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:43,489
Right.

205
00:14:43,490 --> 00:14:48,369
The point of the Holy Grail War is to
get rid of all the other Masters' Servants.

206
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:53,500
Which means that there is no rule stating
that you have to kill the other Masters.

207
00:14:53,950 --> 00:14:57,289
Emiya Shirou, if I may ask...

208
00:14:57,290 --> 00:15:00,500
Do you think that you could
defeat your own Servant?

209
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:05,509
Servants are difficult to defeat,
even if you have a Servant yourself.

210
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:07,429
So what to do?

211
00:15:07,430 --> 00:15:10,140
The answer is simple, is it not?

212
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:13,269
No matter how
powerful the Servant,

213
00:15:13,270 --> 00:15:17,479
if its Master is killed,
the Servant will vanish.

214
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,730
In which case...

215
00:15:19,690 --> 00:15:22,189
Killing the Master
is the quickest way.

216
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:23,900
Exactly.

217
00:15:25,610 --> 00:15:29,409
But what about the opposite case? What
if a Master's Servant is destroyed first?

218
00:15:29,410 --> 00:15:32,699
Only Servants can
touch the Grail, right?

219
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:36,829
That implies that a Master who's lost
their Servant no longer has any value.

220
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:41,669
No, as long as their Command Spells
exist, so do their rights as a Master.

221
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:45,759
So, if there were a Servant that had
lost its Master and had nowhere to go,

222
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,930
it would still have a
chance to rejoin the battle.

223
00:15:49,510 --> 00:15:53,930
It is for that reason that
Masters kill other Masters.

224
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:58,190
Then what if I used up all my
Command Spells right now?

225
00:15:58,560 --> 00:15:59,940
Wait, that's...

226
00:16:00,310 --> 00:16:04,979
True, you would relinquish
your rights as a Master.

227
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:08,766
Although I cannot imagine
a mage using magic as

228
00:16:08,778 --> 00:16:12,980
powerful as a Command
Spell in so wasteful a manner.

229
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:17,199
Any such mage could not
even be called incompetent...

230
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:20,210
they would be no
more than a coward.

231
00:16:22,250 --> 00:16:24,249
Have I convinced you?

232
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:27,720
Then let us go back to the
beginning, Emiya Shirou.

233
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:32,599
If you wish to forfeit your
status as Master, then so be it.

234
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:36,969
Simply use up your Command Spells
and break your contract with Saber.

235
00:16:36,970 --> 00:16:43,309
If you do so, I shall guarantee your
safety until the Holy Grail War's end.

236
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:46,730
Why would I need you
to guarantee my safety?

237
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:54,240
I was dispatched here to oversee
the cycle of Holy Grail Wars.

238
00:16:54,780 --> 00:17:00,500
Safeguarding mages that are no longer
Masters is the overseer's top priority.

239
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:02,500
"Cycle"?

240
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:03,959
Hang on...

241
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:07,500
The Holy Grail War
didn't begin just now?

242
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,589
This is the fifth such war.

243
00:17:10,590 --> 00:17:16,599
The previous one was ten years
ago, making this the shortest cycle yet.

244
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,769
This has happened
four times before?

245
00:17:18,770 --> 00:17:19,770
Yes.

246
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:25,270
With each cycle, the Holy Grail
War has only grown more brutal.

247
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:32,279
Driven by their desires, Masters have
engaged in indiscriminate slaughter.

248
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,279
Indiscriminate slaughter...

249
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:38,869
Then what would happen if
the Grail fell into evil hands?

250
00:17:38,870 --> 00:17:44,119
It is beyond our means to stop
one whom the Grail has chosen.

251
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:48,709
After all, it is an omnipotent,
wish-granting chalice.

252
00:17:48,710 --> 00:17:53,879
If you do not wish that to happen,
Emiya Shirou, win it yourself.

253
00:17:53,880 --> 00:18:00,140
At the very least, if you win, it will
not go to an indiscriminate killer, yes?

254
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:06,020
I have no reason to fight.

255
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:11,489
So you have no interest in
what the Grail's holder does,

256
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:15,530
no matter what atrocities
may be wrought?

257
00:18:15,950 --> 00:18:17,029
That's not...

258
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:20,289
If you have no
reason to fight, so be it.

259
00:18:20,290 --> 00:18:25,999
I take it the events of ten
years ago do not concern you?

260
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,040
Ten years ago?

261
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:28,999
Indeed.

262
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:34,799
At the end of the previous Grail War,
an unworthy Master touched the Grail.

263
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:38,179
I know not of what
that Master wished.

264
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:43,310
All we know is the
resultant disaster.

265
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:44,980
Wait a minute.

266
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,560
Are you saying...

267
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:51,360
I am.

268
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:56,739
The Shinto fire, whose cause
remains officially unknown,

269
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,320
was the result of the
last Holy Grail War.

270
00:19:00,910 --> 00:19:02,120
Emiya-kun!

271
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,749
You said that this
is the fifth one, right?

272
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,879
Has anyone ever
won the Grail, then?

273
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:17,259
One man did indeed
hold the Grail, albeit briefly.

274
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:20,049
What happened to him?

275
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:21,890
Nothing.

276
00:19:22,430 --> 00:19:25,890
That Grail did not
achieve completion.

277
00:19:26,270 --> 00:19:30,400
The result of a foolish man letting
sentiment get the better of him.

278
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:34,029
Simply causing the
Grail to appear is trivial.

279
00:19:34,030 --> 00:19:38,660
Once the seven Servants are
gathered, the Grail will appear in time.

280
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:44,159
As Rin says, it is not necessary
to slay the other Masters.

281
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:47,289
But unless you do so, the
Grail will never be complete.

282
00:19:47,290 --> 00:19:51,419
It chooses the Master
who is worthy of it.

283
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:56,760
That is why this man, who
avoided fighting, did not win the Grail.

284
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:58,969
In other words,

285
00:19:58,970 --> 00:20:01,367
obtaining the Grail is
meaningless unless you

286
00:20:01,379 --> 00:20:03,680
settle things with
the other Masters first.

287
00:20:04,390 --> 00:20:06,778
In the last war, the
Master who was first to

288
00:20:06,790 --> 00:20:09,190
get his hands on the
Grail was a naïve fool.

289
00:20:09,690 --> 00:20:11,769
That is all I have to say.

290
00:20:11,770 --> 00:20:15,109
Will you participate
in the Holy Grail War?

291
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:17,950
Make your decision,
Emiya Shirou.

292
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:30,039
Rejoice, boy.

293
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,580
Your wish will
finally come true.

294
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:36,379
Surely you've realized.

295
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:40,220
Your wish cannot come true
without a clear and distinct evil.

296
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:45,970
Though you may refuse to
admit it, a champion of justice

297
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:49,730
must have an evil to defeat.

298
00:20:54,980 --> 00:20:58,110
Shirou, have you concluded
your business here?

299
00:20:58,990 --> 00:20:59,990
Yeah.

300
00:21:01,030 --> 00:21:02,030
And?

301
00:21:05,780 --> 00:21:08,619
I have decided to
fight as a Master.

302
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:12,370
Will you agree to me
as your Master, Saber?

303
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,090
My agreement is irrelevant.

304
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:19,260
You have been my
Master from the very start.

305
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:24,260
Did I not swear that my
body would be your blade?

306
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,100
Right, in that case...

307
00:21:30,270 --> 00:21:33,520
I will be your Master.

308
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:36,770
I'll be counting on you, Saber.

309
00:21:38,690 --> 00:21:40,900
What? We aren't
supposed to shake hands?

310
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:42,610
It isn't that.

311
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:46,030
I was simply taken by surprise.

312
00:21:49,490 --> 00:21:51,210
Allow me to renew my vow.

313
00:21:51,870 --> 00:21:56,540
So long as the Command Spells are
on your body, I shall serve as your blade.

314
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:01,800
If the Holy Grail War was the
cause of the fire ten years ago,

315
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:06,930
I won't let something like
that ever happen again.

316
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,450
Tohsaka?

317
00:22:26,490 --> 00:22:29,329
No offense, but you should
go home on your own.

318
00:22:29,330 --> 00:22:30,330
Huh?

319
00:22:30,331 --> 00:22:35,459
I brought you here because you
weren't officially my enemy yet.

320
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:38,459
But now, you're a
fellow Master, Emiya-kun.

321
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:41,210
I have no intention of
fighting you, Tohsaka.

322
00:22:43,380 --> 00:22:45,379
I should have known.

323
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:48,220
Jeez, why did I even
bother bringing you here?

324
00:22:48,970 --> 00:22:49,970
Rin.

325
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:51,260
What?

326
00:22:51,770 --> 00:22:55,230
If an easily slain enemy presents itself,
we'd be remiss not to take advantage.

327
00:22:55,890 --> 00:22:58,230
You don't have to tell me that.

328
00:22:58,690 --> 00:23:01,479
If you agree, then act.

329
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,109
Or what?

330
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:05,990
Will you take pity
on that boy again?

331
00:23:07,950 --> 00:23:10,619
Don't tell me you have feel...

332
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:12,620
O-Of course not!

333
00:23:14,750 --> 00:23:15,870
I just, well...

334
00:23:16,370 --> 00:23:18,669
I owe him, you know?

335
00:23:18,670 --> 00:23:22,130
And I can't fight with a clear
conscience until I've repaid him.

336
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:25,380
Complicating things again.

337
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:29,760
In that case, send for me when
you have repaid this debt of yours.

338
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:34,769
Tohsaka? By
"debt", do you mean...

339
00:23:34,770 --> 00:23:35,770
Yes.

340
00:23:36,270 --> 00:23:41,319
Regardless of why you did it, you
used a Command Spell to stop Saber.

341
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:45,399
So I have to go easy on
you to balance the scales.

342
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:48,319
You get hung up on the
weirdest things, Tohsaka.

343
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:51,410
I know that. But
I have no choice.

344
00:23:52,450 --> 00:23:55,200
I hate being
indebted to someone.

345
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,709
You're a good
person, aren't you?

346
00:23:59,710 --> 00:24:01,670
Flattery won't make
me go any easier on you!

347
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:05,960
I know. But I don't want us
to be enemies if I can help it.

348
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:09,180
I like people like you.

349
00:24:11,550 --> 00:24:12,550
See you around.

350
00:24:16,980 --> 00:24:19,600
So, are you done chatting?

351
00:24:24,650 --> 00:24:25,780
Berserker?

352
00:26:07,250 --> 00:26:08,629
Okay, I'll kill you now.

353
00:26:08,630 --> 00:26:09,919
Is he immortal?

354
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,009
Shirou, get back!

355
00:26:11,010 --> 00:26:12,589
Don't you get that
you're just in the way?

356
00:26:12,590 --> 00:26:15,839
Didn't we just decide that
we would fight together?!

357
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:19,140
A disgraceful hind
deserves to be skewered.

